# SYNOPSIS

```usage
touch [-c] [-t time] files
```

# DESCRIPTION

`touch` sets the time each file was last changed to now, making the file if it doesn't exist.

: `-c`
  Don't make a file that doesn't exist; it is an error.
: `-t`
  Use <time>, in seconds since 1970 UTC, instead of now: in decimal, in hexadecimal after `0x`, or in octal after `0`.

# SEE ALSO

ls(1)

# DIAGNOSTICS

The exit string is `touch` if a file couldn't be changed or made, each one reported, such as `touch: x: cannot create: permission denied`.
